---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site.mjs';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="What Biology Lab collects and why: no accounts, Google Analytics usage statistics, no ads, and practice scores kept only in your browser." schemaType="Article"><article class="article"><div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p><em>Last updated: November 12, 2026</em></p><p>Biology Lab ({site.url.replace('https://', '')}) is free to use and never asks you to sign up. This page explains, in plain language, what information is collected when you visit, who collects it, and how you can opt out.</p><h2>No accounts, no forms</h2><p>There are no accounts, logins, or sign-up forms, so we never ask for your name or email address. Everything you type into a calculator, including any DNA sequence, is processed on your own device and is not sent to our servers.</p><h2>Usage statistics (Google Analytics)</h2><p>We use Google Analytics ({site.analyticsId}) to count visits and see which pages and tools are used, so we know what to improve. Google Analytics uses cookies and similar technology to collect information such as the pages you view, how long you stay, the referring site, your approximate location, and your device and browser type. Calculator inputs and practice answers are not sent to Google Analytics. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p><h2>No advertising</h2><p>Biology Lab shows no ads. No advertising code is loaded on any page, and no advertising cookies are set.</p><h2>Cookie choices</h2><p>Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland see a small cookie banner. Until you choose, Google Analytics runs without cookies. <strong>Accept</strong> allows analytics cookies; <strong>Reject</strong> keeps analytics cookie-free. Your choice is stored in your browser for 180 days (under the key <code>cookieConsent</code>), and you can change it at any time with <em>Cookie settings</em> in the footer.</p><h2>Saved in your browser</h2><p>Your best practice scores are saved in your browser’s local storage so you can see your progress next time. They never leave your device, and clearing your browser data removes them. Local storage also keeps your cookie choice (<code>cookieConsent</code>, for 180 days) if you make one. It holds nothing else.</p><h2>Other services</h2><p>Fonts load from Google Fonts, and our hosting provider keeps standard access logs (such as IP address and requested page) to deliver the site and protect it from abuse.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><ul><li><strong>Cookie banner:</strong> use <em>Cookie settings</em> in the footer to accept or reject analytics cookies.</li><li><strong>Cookies:</strong> block or delete cookies in your browser settings. The tools keep working without them.</li><li><strong>Analytics:</strong> install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</li><li><strong>Practice scores:</strong> clear this site’s data in your browser.</li></ul><h2>Students</h2><p>Biology Lab is made for students and does not ask anyone for personal information. Classroom activities are completed on paper or in a teacher’s own assignment, so student work is never sent to this site. The Share to Google Classroom buttons are plain links: nothing loads from Google until someone clicks one, and Google’s own terms then apply. Parents and teachers with questions are welcome to contact us; the <a class="text-link" href="/teachers/">teacher page</a> explains how the site works in class.</p><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>If anything here changes, we will update this page and the date at the top. Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p><div class="related"><a href="/about/">About Biology Lab ↗</a><a href="/">Explore the tools ↗</a></div></article></Layout>
